<Layout title="Drylining Dalkeith | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Dalkeith. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Dalkeith, Midlothian, and the wider EH postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/dalkeith/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Dalkeith and Midlothian" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Dalkeith</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Dalkeith</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Dalkeith, Midlothian, and the wider EH22 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Dalkeith provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Dalkeith (EH22), Midlothian, and the wider council area. Experienced with historic town properties, new build estates, and commercial fit-outs across Midlothian.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Dalkeith</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Dalkeith is Midlothian's largest town with a population of around 20,000 residents in the EH22 postcode area. Home to Dalkeith Palace, the Midlothian council headquarters, and one of Scotland's most attractive historic towns, the area offers a mix of Georgian properties, modern residential developments, and rural commercial sites. This diversity means our drylining contractors work on everything from historic property restorations around Dalkeith Palace to new build developments in the town centre and rural commercial conversions across Midlothian.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Dalkeith's ongoing regeneration projects — including the town centre improvements, the Midlothian Leisure Centre upgrades, and the A6101 corridor enhancements — create consistent demand for commercial drylining services. We deliver partition wall installation, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems for office refurbishments, retail units, healthcare premises, and residential developments throughout the EH22 postcode area. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards Part H and Part T standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Dalkeith</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Dalkeith crew handles everything from single-room domestic renovations on Eastgate to large-scale commercial fit-outs in the town centre — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation across the entire EH22 postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Period property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in historic Georgian properties and listed buildings around Dalkeith Palace and the Old Town area</li> <li><strong>New build handover drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for housing developments in Lasswade, Bonnyrigg, and the Dalkeith town centre regeneration zones</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and restaurant conversions along Eastgate, the town centre, and the M602 corridor</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings require Scottish Building Standards compliance, delivered with full documentation for Midlothian Council building standards</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Office refurbs, healthcare premises, and education facilities throughout the Midlothian area</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential blocks, student accommodation, and hotel conversions near the Edinburgh fringe venues and Midlothian hotel sector</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Dalkeith We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Dalkeith town centre and Eastgate (EH22)</li> <li>Dalkeith Palace and Park (EH22)</li> <li>Lasswade (EH18)</li> <li>Bonnyrigg (EH19)</li> <li>Rosewell (EH22)</li> <li>Newtongrange (EH22)</li> <li>Bushwood and Dalhousie (EH22)</li> <li>Middleton and Newtongrange (EH22)</li> <li>Braehead and Polton (EH22)</li> <li>Gorebridge and Borthwick (EH26)</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Dalkeith Building Standards &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Dalkeith falls under <strong>Midlothian Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town contains several listed buildings, particularly around Dalkeith Palace and the Old Town conservation areas. Many properties are within designated <strong>Dalkeith Conservation Areas</strong>, meaning any internal structural alterations or external drylining insulation may require listed building consent or planning permission. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council building standards surveyors to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a Georgian house on Eastgate to a large commercial fit-out in the town centre — is fully compliant with current Scottish Building Standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Dalkeith Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As a Dalkeith-based drylining team with daily operations across Midlothian, we understand the town's unique demands. From parking permits for town centre sites to working around Dalkeith Palace's conservation restrictions and managing access on the A6101 corridor, our crew knows the area inside out. All operatives are DBS checked, fully uniformed, and experienced in delivering quality work in Dalkeith's historic and rural environments.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/edinburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Edinburgh</a> — 15 minutes via A68</li> <li><a href="/areas/musselburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Musselburgh</a> — 10 minutes via A68</li> <li><a href="/areas/livingston/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Livingston</a> — 30 minutes via A68</li> <li><a href="/areas/peebles/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Peebles</a> — 25 minutes via A7</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <div style="margin-bottom:2rem;"> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What is dry lining and how does it work? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Dry lining is a method of finishing internal walls and ceilings with plasterboard rather than applying several layers of wet plaster. The boards can be fixed directly to brick or blockwork with drywall adhesive, often called the dot and dab method, or screwed to a timber or metal frame. Once the plasterboard is secure, the joints and screw heads are covered with tape and jointing compound. The surface can then be sanded, painted, wallpapered or finished with a thin plaster skim. Dry lining is commonly used in new builds, extensions, renovations and commercial properties. It provides a smooth finish quickly and can also create space for insulation, soundproofing materials, electrical cables and pipework. </div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do I need planning permission for drylining in Dalkeith? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Internal drylining usually falls under permitted development rights and doesn't require planning permission. However, if your property is listed (Dalkeith has several listed buildings around the Palace and Old Town) or within a Conservation Area, you'll need listed building consent for any internal alterations. We advise checking with Midlothian Council's planning department before starting work on period properties.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What are Scottish Building Standards for drylining? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Scottish Building Standards Part H covers heat and energy efficiency, Part T covers ventilation, and Part C covers structural adequacy. All our drylining work in Dalkeith complies with current Scottish Building Standards. For fire-rated walls, we follow the Fire Standard (Part B) and provide full documentation. We also ensure thermal insulation meets the latest Part H requirements, which is particularly important for Dalkeith's older properties with solid stone walls.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> How long does drylining take in Dalkeith? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> A typical single-room drylining job takes 2–3 days for framing and board installation, plus 1–2 days for taping, jointing, and sanding. Larger commercial projects in the town centre or on the A6101 corridor can take 1–4 weeks depending on scale. We work efficiently to minimise disruption, especially on period property restorations around Dalkeith Palace.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do you offer free quotes for Dalkeith projects? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Yes, we offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Dalkeith and Midlothian. We'll assess your property, discuss your requirements, and provide a detailed written quote within 48 hours. Call us on 0800 820 3090 or fill in our contact form to arrange your free site visit.</div> </details> </div> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Dalkeith Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Dalkeith. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Dalkeith Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>
</Layout>
